# text = There was a time when I thought as you do -- at least , I was fully persuaded that home and its affections were the only things that made life tolerable : that , if deprived of these , existence would become a burden hard to be endured ; but now I have no home -- unless you would dignify my two hired rooms at Horton by such a name ;-- and not twelve months ago I lost the last and dearest of my early friends ; and yet , not only I live , but I am not wholly destitute of hope and comfort , even for this life : though I must acknowledge that I can seldom enter even an humble cottage at the close of day , and see its inhabitants peaceably gathered around their cheerful hearth , without a feeling ALMOST of envy at their domestic enjoyment
