# text = I have known governesses who have so completely identified themselves with the reputation of their young ladies for elegance and propriety in mind and manners , that they would blush to speak a word against them ; and to hear the slightest blame imputed to their pupils was worse than to be censured in their own persons -- and I really think it very natural , for my part Do you , ma'am Yes , of course : the young lady's proficiency and elegance is of more consequence to the governess than her own , as well as to the world .
